# Build outputs.
#
# build/bin, not build/. build/darwin holds Info.plist, Info.dev.plist and
# entitlements.plist — the bundle's identity, its minimum system version and its
# hardened-runtime exceptions. Those are sources, and ignoring them meant a
# fresh clone had none of them: `wails build` silently regenerates its own
# defaults (com.wails.<name>, LSMinimumSystemVersion 10.13.0, no privacy usage
# strings), so a release built anywhere but this working copy shipped a
# different app.
build/bin/
release/
elterminalo

# Go
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Frontend
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/wailsjs/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Temp
*.tmp
/tmp/
frontend/package.json.md5

# Local dependencies (built by `make setup-llm`)
deps/

